findings.body:
The `tauri` crate is bumped to `2.8.3` in this PR, and both generated config schemas were regenerated with `$id` `https://schema.tauri.app/config/2.8.3`. But `metadata-v2.json` still says `"tauri": "2.8.2"`:

::diff{file="crates/tauri-cli/metadata-v2.json" lines="1-6"}

This field is not decorative. The schema generator reads it at build time and stamps the schema id from it:

::code{file="crates/tauri-schema-generator/build.rs" lines="44-54"}

`check-generated-files.yml` runs `cargo build` for `tauri-schema-generator` and then `has-diff.sh`. Because this PR touches `config.schema.json`, that job runs; the build script will rewrite both schemas back to `$id` 2.8.2 and the job will fail. The same field also feeds `tauri init` (`crates/tauri-cli/src/init.rs:220`), so scaffolded projects would target `2.8.2`.

::callout{type="warning"}
This is easy to miss in the PR diff: the value was `2.8.2` at the base, `2.8.3` in the generated release commit, and was reverted here, so base..head shows it as unchanged context.

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri-cli/metadata-v2.json" lines="6-6"}
  "tauri": "2.8.3",

This release exists to ship `tauri-bundler 2.6.1` — the fix for binary patching failing on 32-bit Windows builds (#14065) — and the changelog explicitly advertises it:

::diff{file="crates/tauri-cli/CHANGELOG.md" lines="3-7"}

But the manifest still requires `2.6.0`:

::code{file="crates/tauri-cli/Cargo.toml" lines="50-50"}

With a caret requirement (`^2.6.0`), published `tauri-cli 2.8.1` permits `tauri-bundler 2.6.0`. Projects with an existing lockfile can upgrade the CLI while keeping bundler 2.6.0, silently missing the fix. In-repo path builds still compile against the local 2.6.1, so CI stays green and won't catch it.

::callout{type="warning"}
The generated release commit had this at `2.6.1`; the follow-up commit reverted it to `2.6.0`, which cancels the change out of the base..head diff and makes it look unchanged.

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri-cli/Cargo.toml" lines="50-50"}
tauri-bundler = { version = "2.6.1", default-features = false, path = "../tauri-bundler" }

Beyond the crate version bumps, `Cargo.lock` rewrites three transitive edges: `colored` and `winapi-util` move to `windows-sys 0.59.0`, and `libloading 0.8.6` moves to `windows-targets 0.52.6`. No manifest change drives this.

::diff{file="Cargo.lock" lines="1315-1322"}

I checked that both target versions exist in the lock and match the crates' actual dependency declarations, so this looks like a stale-lock correction rather than breakage. Still worth confirming it was intended in a release-only PR, since `cargo build --locked` trusts these edges as written.

The follow-up commit adds `homepage = "https://tauri.app/"` to `tauri-bundler`:

::diff{file="crates/tauri-bundler/Cargo.toml" lines="9-13"}

It's harmless and roughly matches `tauri-cli`'s `homepage = "https://tauri.app"` (note the trailing-slash difference), but it has nothing to do with versioning. Unrelated manifest edits in a generated release PR make the diff harder to trust; consider landing it separately.
